2026-09-08T17:04Z claude note fix: `nextSweepDelayMS` (bootstrap.js) only checked `phase === 'waiting' && candidates === 0` for the idle cadence. Any of the five phases `host.blocked()` returns (`cpu-busy`, `low-memory`, `low-disk`, `storage-unavailable`, `resources-unavailable`) fell through to the 30 s active cadence instead, since none of them is `'waiting'`. Added `SDT_BLOCKED_PHASES` and an `.includes()` check alongside the existing condition. Red-first: reverting the fix reproduces `30000 !== 600000` in the new test. Also corrected a comment on the pre-existing "recovers on the next sweep" test that had asserted the old (buggy) 30 s reschedule as intentional.

